            <ArticleTitle>The value of β-blockers administration during recovery phase of dobutamine stress echocardiography: a review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>723-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/echo.12201</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dobutamine stress echocardiography (DSE) is a successful technique for detection of ischemia in patients with suspected coronary artery disease (CAD). There are some data that administration of β-blocker after peak infusion of dobutamine can improve sensitivity. The goal of this manuscript is to review the current literature in regard to the mechanism and accuracy of post-dobutamine β-blocker administration for ischemia detection. In this review, we present 2 case reports followed by detailed review of the literature.</AbstractText>
